WEBVTT

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.300
<i>This is the base of Mt. Mitsutouge.</i>

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.450
<i>I finally get to challenge myself 
with a real mountain climb.</i>

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:44.200
Fuji-Hakone-Izu National Park
Mitsutouge
Elevation 1786 M

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:44.200
<i>Still, why would they need to 
keep our destination a secret?</i>

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.960
Superb Viewing Location!

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.370
Mt. Mitsutouge 
(Yamanashi Prefecture)

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.540
Say, Hinata!

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.420
What's that stone?

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.800
Let's see... it's called, "Daruma Rock."

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:56.890
Daruma?

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.430
It's a Daruma figure?!

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.950
So, what's written on it?

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:05.300
That's Sanskrit for <i>Aaku</i>, 
which means, "Great Buddha."{not sure why they do the head-tilt after this line...}

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:10.850
There's something written here!

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.860
The Mountain is not a Trashcan!
Regular Route

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.860
"The Mountain is not a Trashcan!"

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:15.650
Mountain Trail

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.650
Season 2 - New Climb 3

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.860
Season 2 - New Climb 3
Climbing the Mountain

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.000
What's the elevation of Mt. Mitsutouge?

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.230
I think it's 1786 meters.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.110
Mt. Takao was 599 meters...

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:42.930
Mt. Mitsutouge
1786 m above sea level

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.710
So it's about three times as high!

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:42.580
Right.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.930
But, the path is easier 
to walk than I expected.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.160
It sure is!

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.730
There are occasional benches too!

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.200
Don't you mean, too many benches?

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.230
<i>This may be simple to beat!</i>

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.990
"Fork Peek"?

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.240
Fork Peek

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.920
What have we here?

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.210
If you peer through the 
fork in that tree trunk,

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.030
you'll see a real pretty—

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:11.310
Pretty what?

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.490
Oh, uh, nothing!

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.620
We'd better hurry! The sun's gonna set!

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.390
She's right.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:18.990
Let's hurry, Aoi-san!

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.700
We have a long way to go!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.060
What's with them all of a sudden?

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.270
Is that Mt. Fuji?!

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.020
Wow, it's like it's right in front of me!

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.300
Hinata, you can see Mt. Fu—

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.470
We've picked the next mountain to climb!

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:42.950
It's a secret!

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.280
<i>Could this be the surprise?</i>

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:49.520
<i>Because I said I'd like to see Mt. Fuji...?</i>

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.620
Aoi!

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.150
What're you doing?

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.570
Hurry on up!

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:54.790
S-Sure!

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.540
<i>For now, I'll pretend not to know.</i>

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.800
<i>Hinata took a lot of effort 
in planning this trip,</i>

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.920
<i>so there may be an even 
more amazing view ahead!</i>

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.560
No Horses Beyond This Point

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.560
"No Horses Beyond This Point"?

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.880
People ride horses up this far?

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.190
Horses are wonderful!

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.940
Hazardous Mountain Trail

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.130
Is it just me, or has the trail 
gotten steeper all of a sudden?

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:30.040
No wonder horses have to turn back.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.000
Be careful, everyone!

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.030
<i>What an incline...</i>

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.520
<i>It's hard to walk through all these rocks...</i>

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.470
<i>I've been taking longer and longer breaks.</i>

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.690
<i>I have to catch up with the others...</i>

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:18.170
<i>Huh? This isn't fun...</i>

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.130
<i>I'm tired...</i>

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.100
<i>My feet hurt...</i>

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.670
<i>My backpack's heavy...</i>

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.360
<i>It's too hard...</i>

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.280
<i>I wanna go home...</i>

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.680
<i>What am I doing in a place like this?</i>

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:34.180
<i>I want to rest on a bench...</i>

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.820
<i>There were so many of them earlier, 
why aren't there any around here?</i>

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.190
Aoi-chan, are you all right?

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.940
Shall we rest for a bit?

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.970
Have you been pushing yourself too much?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.440
Uh, no...

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.000
Guess I can't blame you.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.650
Not when your reward of Mt. Fuji awaits.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.710
Right...

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:02.920
Huh?

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.690
You noticed the surprise, right?

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.930
But you've been pretending 
you didn't, for Hinata's sake.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.560
And though you're too nice to say so, 
you still feel like you'd rather go home.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.330
Like in a marathon, while mountain climbing,

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:19.690
you'll wear yourself out if you 
increase your pace too much.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.940
So, keep a steady pace!

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.800
When you get tired, take a rest!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.940
And eat something sweet!

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.280
Yummy!

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.650
Isn't it?

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.290
Sweets are great when you're exhausted!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.550
It helps to prepare them in advance 
so you can eat right away,

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.660
and also avoid having trash to dispose of.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.830
I see! You really know a lot!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.130
Once you rest and feel better, 
starting walking again.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.120
Slowly, at your own pace.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.300
Shorten your stride if you need to!

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:51.820
Okay!

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.180
That's the spirit!

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.830
Being gloomy just brings others down too.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:58.940
<i>I see...</i>

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.970
<i>That's why Kaede-san always wears a smile.</i>

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.870
Maybe we were a little unreasonable?

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.760
Doing a real mountain like this unexpectedly

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.320
must be pretty tough.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.320
That's true.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:11.700
But...

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.820
- Can you walk?
- Yes!

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.710
I'm sure she'll be fine.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.200
Yeah!

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:21.800
Aoi-chan, want to try these?

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.340
They're collapsible alpenstocks!

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.570
You just go like this, and...

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.090
They're great for maintaining 
balance on mountain trails.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:36.720
Thank you very much!

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:42.980
Shorten my stride, be aware of each step...

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.380
With mountains, you start off in 
forest where you can't see anything,

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:49.680
but once you've climbed 
your way through the trees,

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:51.860
you find great scenery waiting for you.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:57.530
Whenever I see it, I always think,

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.700
"Thank goodness I didn't give up!"

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:03.830
Sorry about the wait!

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.320
Well, we weren't exactly waiting...

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.280
Maybe our pace was a bit much?

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.220
Let's just take our time from now on!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.090
Right!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.890
88 Saints

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:17.040
It reads, "88 Saints".

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.110
They're so cute!

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.520
Cute, how?

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:47.630
<i>Sub-Note: 
Don't drink water straight
 from just any mountain stream. 
You could become ill.{not in the original, but we kinda feel there should be a disclaimer here...}</i>

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:31.360
That's so wild!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.940
Want to try some too, Aoi-chan?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.630
Wow, it's delicious!

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.880
<i>The sunbeams feel great.</i>

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:57.140
<i>It's still rough, but also 
somewhat enjoyable...</i>

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.750
<i>I want to move ahead quickly.</i>

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:02.750
<i>Oh, but I need to take 
my time and not rush...</i>

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:06.410
<i>A cliff?!</i>

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:07.840
<i>We're crossing this?!</i>

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:13.820
<i>I'd be a goner if I fell here...</i>

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:14.650
<i>I'm scared...</i>

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:16.650
<i>What'll I do?</i>

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:19.680
Aoi-chan?

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:20.990
Aoi!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.540
Aoi-san!

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.560
You'll be fine!

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.710
Just walk looking down at your feet.{she definitely doesn't mean to look down over the cliff}

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.040
Then it won't be scary!

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.670
Hinata...

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.430
Hinata-chan's right.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.580
Go forward while watching your feet, 
and without looking around.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:53.590
<i>They're right, this isn't too scary.</i>

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.820
<i>I may be able to make it this way.</i>

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:57.270
Keep going!

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:57.820
Yeah!

00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.490
Easy does it!

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.330
That's the way!

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:14.090
<i>Moving forward, step by step!</i>

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.930
Looking good! You're almost there!

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:26.510
I-I made it...

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.830
You sure did! You're fine now.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.950
See? That was no problem.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:31.690
Right...

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:34.480
Looking back, I feel scared like always,

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.490
but I can manage going one step at a time.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:38.610
That's how it is.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:39.900
Aoi.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:41.570
What is it?

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:42.410
Look.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.050
<i>Mt. Fuji really does look blue, 
like in pictures...</i>

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.930
<i>To think I can view this kind of scenery...</i>

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:10.160
<i>It's even prettier than a photograph...</i>

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.690
<i>I wonder why?</i>

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.650
<i>I know!</i>

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.720
<i>It's because I came this 
far on my own two feet!</i>

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:20.790
Hinata, thank you.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:24.740
Don't tell me you noticed 
the surprise along the way.

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:27.090
That doesn't matter.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.530
Really, thank you.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:36.280
<i>Now I understand why I walked all this way.</i>

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.150
<i>It was to view scenery like this.</i>

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:43.530
Well, everyone, we're almost to the summit!

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.760
Let's keep going!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:45.890
Yeah!

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:49.270
<i>The sky feels wider than a moment ago.</i>

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:51.400
<i>It's incredibly liberating...</i>

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:54.650
<i>I wonder what it'll be like at the summit...</i>

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.030
To Be Continued!
